+Subject: [PATCH] up: EDEN_UP_WAIT_RECLAIM's pass, checkers' fixes on 0970 (the front's switch, off unless set)
+
+Why: two checkers of T181a (13 Nov) read 0970 in source and found:
+- WaitReclaimEvict took GPU-written images that are not downloadable (unbacked, MSAA, trimmed levels,
+  CPU-and-GPU-written) and BadOverlap ones with no write-back, at age 2 and pass after pass;
+- its delete reason started with "gc", so under EDEN_UP_TC_KEEP_REMADE every image it dropped was
+  recorded and kept for good when made again;
+- it ignored EDEN_UP_TC_OOM_SPARE_FRAMES's protection of recent ASTC (CostlyLoad);
+- the pass runs as a deferred Call entry, which rethrows (the 0921 backstop absorbs Method entries only),
+  and it allocates exactly when memory is short: a std::bad_alloc would end the app;
+- in synchronous GPU mode PushCommand blocks the front's helper (with the registry mutex held) until
+  the GPU thread ran the pass, and that thread may be the one waiting.
+
+What:
+- WaitReclaimEvict never takes a GpuModified image (stricter than CollectForBuffer and LoadHoldEvict);
+  reason "wait-reclaim" (not "gc", so EDEN_UP_TC_KEEP_REMADE does not count it); with
+  EDEN_UP_TC_OOM_SPARE_FRAMES=K, CostlyLoad images unused for under 2K frames go only in a third sweep,
+  and only when the front marks the wait urgent (eden_wait_reclaim_request's new `flags`, bit 0);
+  images are deleted one at a time and counted as they go.
+- The queued function catches everything: a throw ends the pass with outcome Failed (5); the cache
+  locks unlock on the way out.
+- QueueWaitReclaim queues nothing in synchronous GPU mode and the request returns 2 then (the front
+  stops asking). In asynchronous mode the GPU thread's queue is unbounded (host_command_queue.h).
+
+No request (the default): nothing here runs. No file here is a translation id input and no name is added
+to TranslationSwitches: KEEPS THE STORE.
